ectional  throughput today  for the light cpu configuration type and  we have a very strong road map to  basically  improve this and you can actually expect  those high  performance through throughput instances  to be on c2 instances  what we are observing is hpc and machine  learning infrastructure are undergoing a  convergence we are actually seeing more  and more machine learning workloads  now using the hpc platform gpus are  hence becoming a very integral part of  hpc  gcp actually offers high performance  gpus on google cloud for machine  learning central computation  and 3d visualization gpus can actually  be added to your  your vm instance type and these vm  insteads are highly configurable because  it has storage  memory bandwidth and it actually acts  like a a regular vm for you  but you can you can attach up to eight  gpus  for these instance range gps will also  work with your gka clusters  and gpu will always for you will also  work with your preemptable vms  which is actually a very common use case  for hpc and ml  now one very important point that i  would like to make is we have a very  strong partnership with nvidia and that  actually helps us  bring the gpus that the the latest and  the greatest gpus  uh that basically nvidia comes up with  on our class platform as  fast as we can today we support the  tesla platform and uh in the future we  are in the very near future we'll be  supporting the nvidia's actually ampere  platform  uh from a bandwidth standpoint we  actually deliver up to 100 gigs on  certain  gpu types today and this is actually in  beta but we have a very very strong road  map coming up  and you can expect that you know the  higher throughput  um that which is very very important for  hpc is going to be showing up  for the gpu machine types in the very  near future uh now cost is actually very  important for for customers have you  mentioned before right so we have  various programs and various options  that's available for customer